  "text": "proprium.commemoratio-omnium-fidelium-defunctorum-missa-iii-evangelium",
  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed — Mass III” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": {
      "translation": "At that time, Jesus said to the multitudes of the Jews, I am the living bread that has come down from heaven. If anyone eat of this bread he shall live forever; and the bread that I will give is My Flesh for the life of the world. The Jews on that account argued with one another, saying, How can this man give us His Flesh to eat? Jesus therefore said to them, Amen, amen, I say to you, unless you eat the Flesh of the Son of Man, and drink His Blood, you shall not have life in you. He who eats My Flesh and drinks My Blood has life everlasting and I will raise him up on the last day."
    }
  },
